IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voc-common`
IMPORT `ctp-core`
IMPORT `voc-seat-insurer`
IMPORT `voc-seat`

-- Cases for the CTP insurer's seat (voc-seat-insurer.l4), the insurer's and nominal defendant's regulative rules in
-- ctp-core.l4, and MIRROR CASES: the same facts asked from the injured person's seat (voc-seat.l4) and from the
-- insurer's, with answers that must agree. Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited texts (the Motor
-- Vehicles Act 1959 as at 2024-11-07 and its Third Party Insurance Regulations 2013; the Civil Liability Act 1936 as at
-- 2023-06-22 and its 2013 Regulations), never copied from the encoding's output.
--
-- Every claim is HYPOTHETICAL, and so are the CPI figures (September 2001 75.0, September 2025 141.0; March 2013 100.0,
-- March 2025 130.0) and State average weekly earnings ($2 000). Clock for the regulative rules: days.

`1 Mar 2026`  MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2026
`15 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 3 2026
`31 Aug 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 8 2026
`10 Sep 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 10 9 2026
`30 Jun 2013` MEANS `the calendar date` 30 6 2013

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- The insurer's questions
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- CASE "Dana's insurer", HYPOTHETICAL: the insurer of the car that hit Dana on a crossing, 31 August 2026.
#ASSERT `Is this claim mine to answer` `31 Aug 2026` `as a direct consequence of the driving of the vehicle` FALSE `insured under a policy under Part 4` TRUE EQUALS `the vehicle's CTP insurer (s 126A(1))`
-- A hit-and-run: the nominal defendant's (s 115), and so the nominal defendant is the respondent.
#ASSERT `Is this claim mine to answer` `31 Aug 2026` `as a direct consequence of the driving of the vehicle` FALSE `not identified after due inquiry and search` TRUE EQUALS `the nominal defendant, because the vehicle was not identified (s 115)`
#ASSERT `the respondent to the claim` `the nominal defendant, because the vehicle was not identified (s 115)` EQUALS `the nominal defendant`
#ASSERT `the respondent to the claim` `the nominal defendant, because the vehicle was uninsured (s 116)` EQUALS `the nominal defendant`
#ASSERT `the respondent to the claim` `the vehicle's CTP insurer (s 126A(1))` EQUALS `the insurer`
-- A claimant hurt when a passenger in the insured car was assaulted by another passenger: not "use" (s 99(3)).
#ASSERT `Is this claim mine to answer` `31 Aug 2026` `in some other way` FALSE `insured under a policy under Part 4` TRUE EQUALS `no CTP claim: the injury was not caused by and did not arise out of the use of a motor vehicle (s 99(3), (3a))`
-- The claimant should have notified by 28 February 2027 (31 August + 6 months, reg 4(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `By when must the claimant have notified me` `31 Aug 2026` `as a direct consequence of the driving of the vehicle` FALSE `insured under a policy under Part 4` TRUE `31 Aug 2026` EQUALS `within 6 months after the accident, that is on or before` (`the calendar date` 28 2 2027)
-- The nominal defendant's claim: as soon as reasonably practicable after 10 September 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the claimant have notified me` `31 Aug 2026` `as a direct consequence of the driving of the vehicle` FALSE `uninsured` TRUE `10 Sep 2026` EQUALS `as soon as reasonably practicable after it became apparent that the vehicle could not be identified or was uninsured, which was on` `10 Sep 2026`
-- May I decline? Arguments: approved form; everything required; access authority; why late; prejudiced.
#ASSERT (NOT (`May I decline to deal with this claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE `it was not late` FALSE))
#ASSERT `May I decline to deal with this claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE `it was not late` FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`May I decline to deal with this claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE `absence of the claimant from the State` FALSE))
#ASSERT `May I decline to deal with this claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE `absence of the claimant from the State` TRUE
-- Can the claimant sue? Not without the medical certificate (a (2)(c) item); yes once (2)(c) and (d) are given, late
-- and unexcused or not (reg 4(3)).
#ASSERT (NOT (`Can the claimant start or continue proceedings` TRUE FALSE TRUE `it was not late` FALSE))
#ASSERT `Can the claimant start or continue proceedings` TRUE TRUE TRUE `none of the reg 4(2)(a) causes` TRUE
-- What I must do: the two s 126A duties.
#ASSERT `What must I do for claimants` TRUE EQUALS LIST `send the claimant (or the claimant's lawyer) a copy of each record or information obtained under the access authority, within 21 days of receiving it (s 126A(4))`, `establish practices and procedures designed to assist claimants to comply with s 126A (s 126A(5))`
#ASSERT `What must I do for claimants` FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
-- Records received 15 March 2026: a copy by 5 April 2026 (15 + 21 = 36; March has 31 days).
#ASSERT `By when must I send the claimant a copy` `15 Mar 2026` EQUALS `the calendar date` 5 4 2026
-- Records received 31 August 2026: 21 September 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I send the claimant a copy` `31 Aug 2026` EQUALS `the calendar date` 21 9 2026

-- Damages for non-economic loss against my insured, accident 1 March 2026, the bands at 1.30 (130 / 100): ISV 45 gives
-- 29 900 + 14 x 3 900 = 84 500; ISV 8 (no exception) nothing.
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can be awarded against my insured` `1 Mar 2026` 60 2000 45 FALSE 0 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 84500
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can be awarded against my insured` `1 Mar 2026` 60 2000 8 FALSE 0 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `none: the injury scale value is 10 or less (s 52(4))`
-- Loss of earning capacity: past 20 000 less a first week of 800 = 19 200; future 100 000, ISV 5 (not over 7, no
-- exception): only the past, 19 200 x 0.8 = 15 360.
#ASSERT `What is the most that can be awarded for loss of earning capacity` 20000 800 100000 5 FALSE 141 75 EQUALS 15360
-- Gratuitous services: a child caring 6 hours a week for 6 months (both the minimum), ISV 11, 26 weeks at $30 (under
-- the $32.50 rate): 6 x 30 x 26 = 4 680, under 4 x 2 000.
#ASSERT `What is the most that can be awarded for gratuitous services` `1 Mar 2026` `a child of the injured person` 11 6 6 26 30 2000 FALSE 130 100 EQUALS 4680

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- The insurer's and the nominal defendant's regulative rules (ctp-core.l4)
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 126A(4): a copy on day 21 is in time; the nominal defendant on day 10 too.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 126A(4) -- the insurer or nominal defendant must send the claimant a copy of each record it obtains under the access authority within 21 days` `the insurer`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `send the claimant a copy of the record or information obtained under the access authority` 21)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 126A(4) -- the insurer or nominal defendant must send the claimant a copy of each record it obtains under the access authority within 21 days` `the nominal defendant`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the nominal defendant` `send the claimant a copy of the record or information obtained under the access authority` 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the insurer, "s 126A(4): ..." (the copy went on day 22)
#TRACE `s 126A(4) -- the insurer or nominal defendant must send the claimant a copy of each record it obtains under the access authority within 21 days` `the insurer` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insurer` DOES `send the claimant a copy of the record or information obtained under the access authority` AT 22
-- s 126A(5): practices and procedures in place.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 126A(5) -- the insurer and the nominal defendant must establish practices and procedures to assist claimants to comply` `the insurer`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `establish practices and procedures to assist claimants to comply with s 126A` 0)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: still owed: the nominal defendant MUST establish practices and procedures (a standing duty with no time)
#TRACE `s 126A(5) -- the insurer and the nominal defendant must establish practices and procedures to assist claimants to comply` `the nominal defendant` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 365)

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- MIRROR CASES: the same facts from both seats
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Who answers (the injured person: "Whom must I give my notice of claim to"; the insurer: "Is this claim mine").
#ASSERT `Whom must I give my notice of claim to` `31 Aug 2026` `as a direct consequence of the driving of the vehicle` FALSE `insured under a policy under Part 4` TRUE EQUALS `Is this claim mine to answer` `31 Aug 2026` `as a direct consequence of the driving of the vehicle` FALSE `insured under a policy under Part 4` TRUE
#ASSERT `Whom must I give my notice of claim to` `31 Aug 2026` `as a direct consequence of the vehicle running out of control` FALSE `uninsured` TRUE EQUALS `Is this claim mine to answer` `31 Aug 2026` `as a direct consequence of the vehicle running out of control` FALSE `uninsured` TRUE
#ASSERT `Whom must I give my notice of claim to` `30 Jun 2013` `as a direct consequence of the driving of the vehicle` FALSE `insured under a policy under Part 4` TRUE EQUALS `Is this claim mine to answer` `30 Jun 2013` `as a direct consequence of the driving of the vehicle` FALSE `insured under a policy under Part 4` TRUE
-- The notice deadline.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` `31 Aug 2026` `as a direct consequence of the driving of the vehicle` FALSE `insured under a policy under Part 4` TRUE `31 Aug 2026` EQUALS `By when must the claimant have notified me` `31 Aug 2026` `as a direct consequence of the driving of the vehicle` FALSE `insured under a policy under Part 4` TRUE `31 Aug 2026`
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` `31 Aug 2026` `as a direct consequence of the driving of the vehicle` FALSE `not identified after due inquiry and search` TRUE `10 Sep 2026` EQUALS `By when must the claimant have notified me` `31 Aug 2026` `as a direct consequence of the driving of the vehicle` FALSE `not identified after due inquiry and search` TRUE `10 Sep 2026`
-- May the insurer decline.
#ASSERT `May the insurer refuse to deal with my claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE `ignorance or mistake of the claimant` TRUE EQUALS `May I decline to deal with this claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE `ignorance or mistake of the claimant` TRUE
#ASSERT `May the insurer refuse to deal with my claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE `inability of the claimant on account of injury` FALSE EQUALS `May I decline to deal with this claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE `inability of the claimant on account of injury` FALSE
-- Proceedings.
#ASSERT `Can I start or continue proceedings` TRUE TRUE FALSE `it was not late` FALSE EQUALS `Can the claimant start or continue proceedings` TRUE TRUE FALSE `it was not late` FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I start or continue proceedings` FALSE TRUE TRUE `none of the reg 4(2)(a) causes` TRUE EQUALS `Can the claimant start or continue proceedings` FALSE TRUE TRUE `none of the reg 4(2)(a) causes` TRUE
-- The 21 days.
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer send me a copy` `15 Mar 2026` EQUALS `By when must I send the claimant a copy` `15 Mar 2026`
-- Non-economic loss (ISV 20: 15 600 at 1.30; ISV 9 with the court using 11: 3 900).
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can I get` `1 Mar 2026` 30 500 20 FALSE 0 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `What damages for non-economic loss can be awarded against my insured` `1 Mar 2026` 30 500 20 FALSE 0 141 75 130 100
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can be awarded against my insured` `1 Mar 2026` 30 500 20 FALSE 0 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 15600
#ASSERT `What damages for non-economic loss can I get` `1 Mar 2026` 30 500 9 TRUE 11 141 75 130 100 EQUALS `What damages for non-economic loss can be awarded against my insured` `1 Mar 2026` 30 500 9 TRUE 11 141 75 130 100
-- Loss of earning capacity (280 800, as worked in voc-cases-injured.l4).
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for loss of earning capacity` 52000 1000 300000 12 FALSE 141 75 EQUALS `What is the most that can be awarded for loss of earning capacity` 52000 1000 300000 12 FALSE 141 75
#ASSERT `What is the most that can be awarded for loss of earning capacity` 52000 1000 300000 12 FALSE 141 75 EQUALS 280800
-- Gratuitous services (8 000, the 4 x SAWE limit).
#ASSERT `What is the most I can get for my family's care` `1 Mar 2026` `the spouse of the injured person` 15 10 8 30 40 2000 FALSE 130 100 EQUALS `What is the most that can be awarded for gratuitous services` `1 Mar 2026` `the spouse of the injured person` 15 10 8 30 40 2000 FALSE 130 100
#ASSERT `What is the most that can be awarded for gratuitous services` `1 Mar 2026` `the spouse of the injured person` 15 10 8 30 40 2000 FALSE 130 100 EQUALS 8000
